yments in equal increments on a pay period basis until such time as the employee receives all severance pay due. In such a case, the payment will amount at least to the base pay of a regular biweekly pay period.","type":"paragraph","workbench_component_id":"17fcf8d9-7ff2-5416-985a-b058951aa15a"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"2.110.070","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/2.110.070","content_hash":"5c1e63b658a63c4f2243c34450fea49b7169eb76ceb5676c631f795f30861555","heading":null,"ordinal":21,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:2.110.070:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:2.110.070:block:21","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/2.110.070","text":"(5) Whether employees can draw both severance pay and unemployment compensation benefits will be dependent upon applicable State law.","type":"paragraph","workbench_component_id":"425a0a8f-2494-52bb-8ed7-1829b867e1dd"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"2.110.070","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/2.110.070","content_hash":"c0a038f853db2b602678ce308577d8c44388f12644446ee8b9ac80ded392df45","heading":null,"ordinal":22,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:2.110.070:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:2.110.070:block:22","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/2.110.070","text":"(6) Employees who resign, retire or are terminated for cause shall not be eligible to receive severance pay. (Ord. 20206 § 21, 9-10-19.)","type":"paragraph","workbench_component_id":"9b72c94c-c61c-5186-b873-9de60330fb93"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"2.110.070","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/2.110.070","content_hash":"d41ed969f4f69b83f291afab2ee5ae1882fde020e8c715e6898622fece7de356","heading":null,"ordinal":23,"parent_source